## Summary

Publishes a public, deidentified synthetic derivative of the GroundSignal patient-evaluation pilot.

Included:
- 12 public case cards;
- 3 runnable dynamic-interview scripts;
- 6 synthetic fixed-replay cases with 10 independent checkpoints;
- local runner, collection workbook, protocol, PDF operation guide, and fail-closed release validator;
- aggregate smoke, workbook, and privacy-gate records.

Privacy boundary:
- no original patient dialogue text or source identifiers;
- no completed review JSON/HTML, reviewer metadata, evidence spans, original turn IDs, or redaction maps;
- no exact-source replay contexts, real model transcripts, local run logs, screenshots, or clinical adjudication records.

Trust boundary:
- `formal_approval=false`;
- `clinical_gold=false`;
- the privacy gate reduces release risk but does not prove zero re-identification risk or clinical validity.

All files are confined to `medical/patient-eval/pilot/real-dialogue-derived-v0.1/`.
